DEBT COLLECTED 2026-08-14 (commit d1c300b) — and collecting it found that the slice was BROKEN.
  Their fix to `toint-on-a-non-integer-diverges` closed it by making both lanes ABORT, which turns
  isInt's round-trip into a landmine: isNumeric runs on every CSV field and `seconds` is `3.1`.
  Measured: isNumeric("3.1") panics. The file BUILT against their fixed main and would have died
  on the first request. Rewritten as a digit walk with the same canonical-form semantics, 14-row
  table, both lanes byte-identical.
  viewRoute stays on `split`, for a NEW reason: `String.length` answers BYTES on build-rust while
  substring counts CHARACTERS, so `html.substring(at, html.length)` panics mid-request on a page
  with any non-ASCII character — and the panic poisons the server for every request after. Filed
  as `string-length-counts-bytes-not-characters` (27c47f206), no fix branch: which unit `length`
  answers is a language decision. `joinFrom` IS gone — mkString replaces it.
  Also closed a divergence nobody had measured: `/view/` bare answered 410 here and 404 in Rust.
  RE-VERIFIED after all of it: 1892/1892 cells identical, /view byte-identical on a live, a bogus
  and an empty token, 0 panics. Only the two headers the .ssc runtime adds itself still differ.
blocker-before-any-switch: the .ssc server binds ALL interfaces (`*:8412`) while the Rust
  console binds `127.0.0.1`. Reachable from the LAN only because the host firewall refuses
  the connection today — that is not the protection to rely on. `serve(port)` must take a
  bind address, or the process must be confined, BEFORE these routes move to it. Measured
  with lsof: `pmL *:8412` against `rozum-gateway 127.0.0.1:8411`.
